BEYOND-MINIMUM (full web fidelity — not just the 8 required items)
  - All 7 web SAFETY_ROWS ported in web order, each row = title + info value-badge + description + Docs link,
    using the web i18n keys (safetySettings.rows.quietHoursEnabled / quietHoursStart / quietHoursEnd /
    alertDigestMode / criticalFlashEnabled / tabBadgeEnabled / apiSuspended .title/.description).
  - Value badges localized: On/Off, Active/Suspended, digest instant/hourly/daily, em-dash for unset,
    and verbatim HH:MM window times (SafetyValue.localized/.literal + SafetyValueBadge, web Badge variant="info").
  - loading / empty / error data states implemented (SafetyPageModel.Phase + listingBody) even though the
    manifest declares only `success` — never renders a blank region (loading skeleton, ContentUnavailableView,
    error + Retry).
  - HIG/a11y: combined row accessibility labels, header traits, Docs-link labels + hints; Dynamic Type via
    system fonts; light/dark/increased-contrast via Color.TS tokens; SwiftUI-native (no web cloning).
  - Navigation: SafetyPageRoute + View.safetyPageDestination() registered on the settings NavigationStack;
    SafetyPageLinkRow added to AppSettingsView (web sub-route /settings/safety).
  - The web opt-in <AISafetySettingExplainer> panel is OUT of scope here (separate AI parity unit; the manifest
